# Rightis: check before generating a real person

Rightis (https://rightis.org) is a public registry of identity rights. When code
generates or edits the face, voice or persona of a real person or a registered
character, add a Rightis check on the server, before the generation call, and act on
`next_action`. The path to use always goes through a licence.

Not permission:
- `decision: "allowed"` is not free use. A licence request in those scopes is approved
  without the holder reviewing it if the fee clears their floor. Still request it.
- `decision: "unspecified"` means the holder said nothing. Not a yes.
- `next_action.type: "not_registered"` means not in the registry. Not cleared.
- A failed lookup (any `RightisError`: network, timeout, 5xx, 429, 402) is not
  "not registered". Fail closed and do not generate.

| decision | next_action.type | Code | Tell the user |
|---|---|---|---|
| `allowed` | `request_license` | Block until a licence is active | Pre-approved, licence still required |
| `requires_approval` | `request_license` | Block until approved | The holder decides each request |
| `unspecified` | `request_license` | Block, ask the holder | Holder has not said; not a yes |
| `denied` | `stop` | Do not generate | The holder refuses this use |
| `null` | `not_registered` | Do not generate | Not registered; not cleared |
| `null` | `describe_use` | Re-ask with use fields | (internal) |

Most restrictive wins: `denied > unspecified > requires_approval > allowed`. Also read
`unmapped`, `training` (separate right; pass `for_training: true`) and `notes`.

```ts
import { Rightis, RightisError } from '@rightis/sdk'; // npm install @rightis/sdk

const rightis = new Rightis(); // server only; reads RIGHTIS_SECRET_KEY, keyless resolve without it
const r = await rightis.rights.check({
  rights_id: 'BR-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX',
  use_type: 'instagram ad',
  ai_methods: ['image_generation'], // video_generation, voice_synthesis, style_transfer
  asset_types: ['face'],            // face | voice | style | image
  territory: ['US'],
});
// r.next_action.type: request_license | stop | not_registered | describe_use
```

- Go path: the app holds a licence code for this person and use,
  `rightis.licenses.verify({ license_public_code })` returns `valid: true`, then
  generate, then `rightis.usage.log([...])`.
- Only a name: `rightis.rights.search(name, { limit: 5 })`. No match is not clearance.
- No `isAllowed()` helper exists on purpose. Do not write one.
- CLI: `npx rightis check BR-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX --use "instagram ad" --asset face --public`
  (`--asset` and `--method` repeatable, `--training`, `--json`). Exit 0 for every decision.
- Keyless MCP: `https://rightis.org/api/public-mcp/mcp` (`rights_lookup`, `rights_search`, `registry_info`).

Docs: https://rightis.org/en/developers and
https://rightis.org/en/developers/guides/real-person-likeness
